<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    A function decompiled alone returns what its callers read after the call
    (option callerreads, kuna_callerreads.rs). Issue #843.

    The script loads callerreads_x86_64_gcc_O2 (gcc -O2, source callerreads.c
    beside it). triple is `gi = a * 3; return gi;`, compiled to
    `lea (%rdi,%rdi,2),%eax; mov %eax,gi(%rip); ret`, the same code as a
    function that only stores. keep loads `*p` into eax, stores it to gj and
    `x + 1` to gi, and returns it. same tail-calls strcmp. Upstream's onlyOpUse
    refuses a return value the function also stores or that comes straight from
    a call, so each prints void, while main reads eax after each call. scale
    stores `a * 5` from eax too, but main ignores its result.

    Pass 1 (option off) reproduces the defect: every function prints void.
    Pass 2 (the default) decodes main from the address each call returns to,
    which the Listing files, finds eax read before it is written, and forces
    the return the way decompile-all does: triple, keep and same return int.
    scale stays void.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
